CALIBRATION & SAFETY INTEGRITY FINDINGS:
1. Raw Data Ingestion: Ingested directly from reports/sta_cpm_raw_measurements.csv
   parsed from genuine OpenSTA 3.1.0 runs across discrete Sky130 Liberty libraries.
2. Jitter and Setup Inclusion: Both flip-flop setup time (250 ps) and clock jitter
   budget (350 ps) are fully subtracted from available wavefront propagation time.
3. Negative-Slack Safety Audit: Under severe cold-slow sag (SS 1.40V, -40°C), where MAC
   slack drops to -20.74 ns, the CPM replica delay (28.5 ns) exceeds cycle budget,
   guaranteeing margin collapses strictly to 0 and timing_hazard asserts immediately.
4. Bounded Optimistic Margin: The maximum timing overestimation is strictly bounded
   at 0.0 ps. The target 2-tap deadband (420.0 ps) safely absorbs
   this bound with positive remaining setup margin under all valid operating points.
